ess_group, which the harness docstring names as 'the single source of truth' for reaping a timed-out grounding child + its group (bug d843). The plan's Hardened Execution bullet re-specifies this exact SIGTERM->kill->reap-the-group behavior, including the non-POSIX cross-platform fallback, as new bespoke logic. reap_process_group already provides the grace/SIGKILL sequence, the ESRCH/EPERM (ProcessLookupError/PermissionError) race guards, the bounded post-kill drain with leaked-PID logging, and the non-POSIX proc.kill() fallback — none of which the bespoke _terminate reproduces (it lacks the bounded-drain leak log and guards ProcessLookupError only loosely).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0af3779b69e411a6","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope > Hardened execution, bullet 4 ('terminate then kill and reap the whole group ... on non-POSIX ... use the stdlib's cross-platform terminate->kill'); src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py:282-342 (_run/_terminate)","norm_id":"nf1c18579b6bbc37d","priority":0.8889,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A timed-out or overflowing config-inspect child spawns a pipe-holding grandchild: the bespoke reaper's 1s fixed grace and missing bounded-drain leak logging diverge from the tuned, race-guarded shared reaper, risking orphaned groups or unlogged leaks","A future fix to the shared reaper (another d843-class race) will not propagate to the corroborator's private copy"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the Hardened Execution section, replace the hand-rolled 'terminate then kill and reap the whole group' language with 'reap the child group via the shared rebar._proc.reap_process_group reaper (bug d843 single source of truth), passing the corroborator's grace/drain constants and logger', and change _terminate to call reap_process_group instead of open-coding killpg/SIGTERM/SIGKILL.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asser